        "original_id": "ce44909c-b1de-5604-ac2b-f1686622ce5f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Royal Commission into Drug Trafficking, New South Wales Police, The Honoured Society, 'Ndrangheta\n- Places: New South Wales, Australia, Melbourne\n- Topics: Drug trafficking, organized crime, police-crime links\n\nFacts:\n- From 1977 to 1979, the Royal Commission into Drug Trafficking, also called the Woodward Royal Commission, operated in New South Wales, Australia.\n- The Royal Commission into Drug Trafficking investigated drug trafficking in New South Wales.\n- The Royal Commission into Drug Trafficking examined links between the New South Wales Police and Mafia groups.\n- The Honoured Society is a Calabrian 'Ndrangheta criminal confederation.\n- The Honoured Society started in Melbourne.\n- The Honoured Society is currently active across Australia.",
